  "worked_solution": "Using the commutative law, we can replace the phrase \"$x$ is positive and it is rational\" with the phrase \"$x$ is rational and it is positive.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is rational, and $x$ is rational and it is positive.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"$x$ is rational and $x$ is rational, and it is positive.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"$x$ is rational and $x$ is rational\" to just \"$x$ is rational.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is rational, and it is positive.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely:\n\n\"$x$ is rational and positive.\"",
